<!--
The document layout wrapping every route: a thin use of the shipped <SiteLayout>
shell, which carries the full beet chrome (head/header/sidebar/footer + the body
`page` + color-scheme class). The layout middleware transcludes each route's body
in as SiteLayout's default-slot child, so it lands in <main> with no relay here;
<LiveReloadScript/> and <Wasm/> append to the head chrome, the `nav` links name
this site's own sections, and the sidebar override excludes the `export` route.

<Wasm/> is what makes the served page a launch: the browser boots the wasm
`beet` binary on this same entry (`main.bsx` read through the `/repo` store the
entry publishes) and dispatches its `serve` command under `--server=dom`,
opening at the page's own url, so the page's world runs in the tab and its
event scripts (`routes/counter.bsx`) run on click.
-->
<SiteLayout>
	<LiveReloadScript slot="head"/>
	<Wasm src="/wasm/beet-ui.wasm" repo="/repo" entry="main.bsx" server="dom" route="serve" slot="head"/>
	<Link slot="nav" href="/recipes" variant=ButtonVariant::Text>Recipes</Link>
	<Link slot="nav" href="/guides" variant=ButtonVariant::Text>Guides</Link>
	<Link slot="nav" href="/blog" variant=ButtonVariant::Text>Almanac</Link>
	<RouteSidebar home=false exclude={["export"]} slot="sidebar"/>
</SiteLayout>
